in The Witcher 3 one of the most  important tools you have at your  disposal are Geralt potions while  they're not necessary to your survival  in the beginning of the game they become  much more vital as you progress so it's  a good idea to start farming for their  crafting ingredients early  fortunately the games first area white  orchard is a great place to start  stockpiling in the beginning of the game  you have the ability to craft only four  potions swallow cat thunderbolt and  white honey swallow is a potion that  accelerates your vitality regeneration  cat lets you see in the dark and is  handy during the night or in dark areas  filled with dangerous creatures Thunder  ball creases your attack power for an  added defensive edge in combat and white  honey clears your body of all toxicity  and cancels all active potion effects  little more on that later so how do you  make potions  well potions require three kinds of  ingredients the most essential of these  ingredients are herbs which are found  all around the environment as rule of  thumb you should always collect as many  as possible a great place to get a whole  bunch in white or treat it just outside  the herbalist college though if you ever  need specific herbs such as some  honeysuckle for the white honey potion  you can always buy them from the  herbalist as well the second type of  ingredient you need to craft a potion is  alcohol a consistent ingredient that  appears in all the potions I mentioned  earlier is dwarven spirit you can  usually find some in smuggler caches and  treasure chests scattered around the map  they can also be bought from any white  orchard merchants but a smart thing to  do is to buy a crafting manuscript from  the herbalist so you can make your own  for much cheaper the third type of  ingredient that appears in potion  crafting recipes is moths through body  parts these require some time to get  since you can't really find a place to  buy them in the beginning the big one  you need in white orchard though are  drowner brains for the swallow potion  drowners are the blue humanoid sea  monster folk that are usually found near  water common locations in white orchard  include the southern shore line near the  ransac village the swamp lands to the  south of the nilfgaardian garrison and  along the shoreline to the left of the  Ford signpost knowing those essential  ingredients you should be good to start  making potions but before you do there  are a couple of important things to keep  in mind each potion has something called  a toxicity amount taking a potion will  contribute this amount to Gerald's  overall toxicity level which totals at  100 so always be mindful of how many  potions you consume  lastly when you successfully craft a  potion you typically get a stock of  three what you made you meditate and  have any kind of hard liquor in your  inventory any stock of potions you have  will fully replenish absolutely make  sure to do this whenever you can so you  don't have to farm all those crafting  materials again I hope this helps you on  your ways you continue to play through  and explore the world of The Witcher 3  Wild Hunt
 

